================================================================================================
(3)  THE PRICE:  how much Hamiltonian simulation does the filter need?
================================================================================================
  K is built from e^{iHs} at a range of s. A discretised filter uses
  n_times distinct evolution times, EVERY CYCLE. Fidelity of the
  discretised K against the ideal one, and the cooling it achieves:

    n_times  rel err vs ideal     final E  % to ground
  ----------------------------------------------------
          8            1.1255    -0.42674       -55.6%
         16            0.7310    -0.29631       -76.3%
         32            0.0031    -1.37062        94.3%
         64            0.0000    -1.37148        94.5%
        128            0.0000    -1.37148        94.5%

  Each of those n_times entries is a distinct Hamiltonian evolution, needed
  once per cycle. The protocol exists because phase estimation was too deep
  to run; if the repair puts Hamiltonian simulation back inside every cycle,
  the fix costs the very thing the protocol was avoiding. That is the honest
  closing statement, and it is stronger than 'use a filter'.
